',title:'Title',rate_header:'Rate your experience with this Interpreter',rating1:'Interpreter not turned up',rating2:'The interpreter does not answer calls',rating3:'Interpreter met too late',rating4:"The interpreter's language skills were not in order",rating5:"The interpreter's behavior did not live up to expectations",rating6:'Wrong language / dialect',rating7:'Not the ordered named interpreter',rating8:'Not the ordered gender',rating9:'Service in connection with order',rating10:'Change of booking',rating11:'Booking ok',rating12:'Booking ok but dissatisfied',rating13:'The citizens did not show up',schedule:'Schedule',written:'Written',of:'of',payment1:'You are about to pay the sums of',payment2:'to complete this booking',country:'Country',error_uppercase:'Password must contain uppercase character',error_lowwercase:'Password must contain lowercase character',error_number:'Password must contain number',error_alpha_numeric:'Password must contain non alpha numeric character',error_length:'Minimum of 6 characters',error_password_match:'Confirm password must match password',time:'Time',welcome_text:'Welcome To Sprogteam',account_text:'Your account has been created',evaluate_text:'We will first evaluate your account before it can be used',add_language_text:'Add the language you master 100% by clicking the button below',rebook_text:'Booking was rejected by translator',again:'Again',percentage_text:'You will get',create:'Create',an:'an',offer:'offer',now:'now',file:'File',selected:'Selected',delete:'Delete',gig:'Gig',package:'Package',description:'Description',hour:'Hour',next:'Next',basic:'Basic',standard:'Standard',premium:'Premium',frequently:'Frequently',asked:'Asked',questions:'Questions',previous:'Previous',gallery:'Gallery',upload:'Upload',submit:'Submit',payment:'Payment',list_empty:'List is empty swipe down to reload',no_payment_id:'No payment ID is associated with your account',no_account_number:'No account number is assocaited with your account',bank:'Bank',start_verify:'start verifying your account',document:'Document',type:'Type',option:'Option',international:'International',passport:'Passport',national:'National',identity:'Identity',card:'Card',driver:'Driver',license:'License',certificate:'Certificate',new_id:'We rquire you to upload a valid means of Identification to verify your account',clear_document:'Upload a clear image of your document',click_to_add_payment:'Payment Details is missing from your Account, Click here to add it now',no_payment:'No Payment details Found',search:'Search',sellers:'Sellers',no_result:'No result found for',yet:'Yet',found:'found',booking_for_another:'Booking for another participant',transportation:'Transportation',translator_is_free:'Seller is free for this period',translator_is_not_free:'Seller is not free for this period',awaiting:'Awaiting',response:'Response',task:'Task',direct:'Direct',uploaded:'Uploaded',deadline:'Deadline',click_here:'Click here to upload certificate of authorization',mastery:'Mastery',register_service:'Register the services you want to offer.',to:'To',start:'Start',translating:'Translating',service:'Service',message:'Message',success:'Success',success_mgs:'Payment Successful',freelancer:'Freelancer',review:'Review',negotiate:'You can edit price to negotiate',account_completion:'You can add another language or click the button below to complete your profile creation',done:'Done',otp_text:'Please enter the 4 digit code sent to',email_text:'Enter your email to get started',quote:'Quote',get:'Get',started:'Started',menu:'Menu',quotes:'Quotes',jobs:'Jobs',acceptable:'Acceptable',behaviour:'Behaviour',privacy:'Privacy',policy:'Policy',and:'and',data:'Data',support:'Support',reset:'Reset',your:'Your',personal:'Personal',verify:'Verify',enter:'Enter',let:'Let',sign:'Sign',in:'In',up:'Up',please:'Please',here:'Here',forgot:'Forgot',dont:"Don't",have:'Have',professional:'Professional',team:'Team',blog:'Blog',possible_name:'Preferred Name',note_on_bill:'Note on bill',new:'New',end:'End',handbook_contact:'Contact the interpreter user',handbook_contact_details:'If, as an interpreter, you know the person you are interpreting for, you must contact the office as soon as possible and have the interpretation rearranged. The interpreter must act as objectively as possible, and if the interpreter has knowledge of the non-Danish-speaking person, this can interfere with the result of the interpretation. In addition, as an interpreter, you must not have any personal or financial interest in various interpretations, as this could interfere with the objectivity of the interpretation.',handbook_linguistic:'Linguistic qualifications',handbook_linguistic_details:'If, as an interpreter, you know the person you are interpreting for, you must contact the office as soon as possible and have the interpretation rearranged. The interpreter must act as objectively as possible, and if the interpreter has knowledge of the non-Danish-speaking person, this can interfere with the result of the interpretation. In addition, as an interpreter, you must not have any personal or financial interest in various interpretations, as this could interfere with the objectivity of the interpretation.',handbook_knowledge:'Knowledge of the person to be Interpreter',handbook_knowledge_details:'If, as an interpreter, you know the person you are interpreting for, you must contact the office as soon as possible and have the interpretation rearranged. The interpreter must act as objectively as possible, and if the interpreter has knowledge of the non-Danish-speaking person, this can interfere with the result of the interpretation. In addition, as an interpreter, you must not have any personal or financial interest in various interpretations, as this could interfere with the objectivity of the interpretation.',handbook_doubt:'Doubts about the process',handbook_doubt_details:'If, as an interpreter, you know the person you are interpreting for, you must contact the office as soon as possible and have the interpretation rearranged. The interpreter must act as objectively as possible, and if the interpreter has knowledge of the non-Danish-speaking person, this can interfere with the result of the interpretation. In addition, as an interpreter, you must not have any personal or financial interest in various interpretations, as this could interfere with the objectivity of the interpretation.',handbook_location:'Location',handbook_location_details:'If, as an interpreter, you know the person you are interpreting for, you must contact the office as soon as possible and have the interpretation rearranged. The interpreter must act as objectively as possible, and if the interpreter has knowledge of the non-Danish-speaking person, this can interfere with the result of the interpretation. In addition, as an interpreter, you must not have any personal or financial interest in various interpretations, as this could interfere with the objectivity of the interpretation.',handbook_ability:'Ability',handbook_ability_details:'If, as an interpreter, you know the person you are interpreting for, you must contact the office as soon as possible and have the interpretation rearranged. The interpreter must act as objectively as possible, and if the interpreter has knowledge of the non-Danish-speaking person, this can interfere with the result of the interpretation. In addition, as an interpreter, you must not have any personal or financial interest in various interpretations, as this could interfere with the objectivity of the interpretation.',handbook_drugs_and_tobacco_products:'Drugs and Tobacco Products',handbook_drugs_details:'As an interpreter, you must not be under the influence in any way during interpretation. Furthermore, interpreters must under no circumstances use tobacco products during interpretation, including cigarettes, snus, etc. Finally, interpreters must respect the facilities they visit in connection with on-site interpretation, their smoking policies, and refrain from smoking in places where it is not allowed.',handbook_dress_code:'Dress Code',handbook_dress_code_details:'Interpreters must dress appropriately for on-site and video interpretations. This means that challenging or offensive attire is not allowed. Specifically, short skirts/shorts, bare midriffs, deep necklines, bare shoulders, T-shirts with offensive slogans, etc., are not permitted.',handbook_confidentiality:'Confidentiality',handbook_confidentiality_details:'As an interpreter, one of the most important aspects of the job is confidentiality. This duty has no statute of limitations and therefore does not cease after the completion of a job or task. A breach of this confidentiality duty results in immediate termination.',handbook_neutrality:'Neutrality',handbook_neutrality_details:'As an interpreter, you must not allow yourself to be emotionally influenced, either in the form of sympathies or antipathies. However, being neutral and impartial does not mean that you should act mechanically or uninterested, but that you as an interpreter constantly adhere to your task and role clearly and professionally. You must therefore refrain from: 1. Proposing questions 2. Assessments 3. Proposing the order of the questions 4. Other comments on how the conversation should proceed according to you.',handbook_your_right_as_translator:'Your Rights as a Translator',handbook_your_right_as_translator_details:"As an interpreter, it is also important that your work tasks are respected. That means that as an interpreter, you have full right to object if you are imposed with other functions or tasks during interpretation by others. This applies both if the imposed tasks come from authorized personnel such as doctors and counselors, but also the citizens; if, for example, a citizen asks you to advocate for their case by omitting information or by answering for them, you also have full right to object. As an interpreter, one must be able to politely object to all involved parties if one senses that one's position is threatened, or if the communicative situation is deteriorating.",handbook_right_perspective:'Providing the Right Perspective',handbook_right_perspective_details:"Interpreters will often encounter situations where cultural mediation is necessary. In some situations, a citizen may have a generalized view related to their origin, country, or background in general. Here, the interpreter must be able to distinguish between the individual's viewpoint and what can be assumed generally. Thus, as an interpreter, you should have a broader perspective and clarity about the most widespread norms in your own culture in order to contextualize this in the conversation. Cultural mediation can be of great importance in assessments of work capacity, in rehabilitation cases, etc., which the interpreter should be aware of.",handbook_emotional_scenarios:'Emotional Scenarios',andbook_emotional_scenarios_details:'This aspect relates to interpretations in emotionally charged situations, where individuals being interpreted for have lost control, cry or even sob, are frustrated, or otherwise outwardly reactive. An example of such a situation may be interpretations in involuntary placements, where children cry and parents shout loudly in anger or appear threatening. It may happen that the family has expectations of the interpreter, which can feel very intrusive. Ideally, the interpreter should be able to handle these situations without starting to cry, losing track, or visibly being affected by the situation. Ethically, as an interpreter, one should refrain from interpretations in these situations if one does not feel robust enough or for other reasons cannot handle the task.',handbook_relational_ethics_therapy_and_treatment:'Relational Ethics Therapy and Treatment',handbook_relational_ethics_therapy_and_treatment_details:"Interpretations in therapy and treatment require openness, patience, and empathy, as interpreters may come to interpret for fragile or weakened individuals, who sometimes do not have prospects for improvement. Due to impaired vision, hearing, or no mobility, citizens may seem absent. This may require many repetitions from the interpreter's side, and it must therefore be ensured that the citizen has understood the message, despite the situation. The interpreter should focus on eye contact with the citizen to assess whether it is necessary to repeat any of the information. In addition, the interpreter must be careful not to raise their voice during repetitions but try to speak more slowly and clearly to avoid any potentially provocative behavior, even though it is not intentional. It would be ethically unsound for an interpreter to become irritated, both towards the citizen and the therapist.",handbook_burndens_and_negative_consequences_of_interpretations:'Burden and Negative Consequences of Interpretations',handbook_burndens_and_negative_consequences_of_interpretations_details:"If you come from the same country as a traumatized citizen, you may recognize situations and sufferings that the citizen describes. In these situations as an interpreter, you may be deeply affected by what you are interpreting, and your own memories may unconsciously come into play. However, interpreters have no outlet for the emotions the traumatized person's story may evoke. In the worst case, this may result in the interpreter beginning to experience some of the same symptoms as the traumatized person \u2013 so-called secondary traumatization. This can be physical symptoms such as nightmares, headaches, stomach pains, and difficulty sleeping, but it can also be reduced control over one's emotions, which can be expressed as anxiety, anger, and mistrust towards the environment. The risk of secondary traumatization is greatest if you often interpret for traumatized individuals. As an interpreter, you must be aware of these risks and be prepared to seek advice and supervision well in advance. If you are not aware of the unconscious processes, you may in the worst case lose empathy, become cynical, and irritated. It would be ethically wrong to continue with the interpretation, as this could potentially harm interpreter work, cooperation, and ultimately oneself.",handbook_password:'Password',handbook_password_details:'Sprogteam encourages our users to change their password every 3 months to optimize IT security.',professional_text:'We provide professional assistance to your communication!',solid_text:'Our solid platform.',solid_text_details:'At Sprogteam we offer interpretation and translation in many varieties and languages. We provide professional translations and interpretations in more than 60 languages and dialects, we are also happy to accommodate any need that you may have, using our great network. We offer both generalists and specialists, in addition to a wide range of other relevant language and cultural services, that you can find listed at the bottom of this page. Please do not hesitate to contact us with whatever you may need or be curious about.',faq_account:'Is creating an account on Team is free?',faq_account_details:'From here we offer interpretation and translation in all guises and in all languages. Our skilled and versatile interpreters can provide over 60 languages \u200b\u200band dialects,and we are happy to activate our large network if you have other special needs. We offer both generalists and specialists in addition to a strong range of other relevant language and cultural services listed at the bottom of the page. ',faq_register:'How can I register?',faq_register_details:'From here we offer interpretation and translation in all guises and in all languages. Our skilled and versatile interpreters can provide over 60 languages \u200b\u200band dialects,and we are happy to activate our large network if you have other special needs. We offer both generalists and specialists in addition to a strong range of other relevant language and cultural services listed at the bottom of the page. ',faq_mainservice:'What are the main services?',faq_mainservice_details:'From here we offer interpretation and translation in all guises and in all languages. Our skilled and versatile interpreters can provide over 60 languages \u200b\u200band dialects,and we are happy to activate our large network if you have other special needs. We offer both generalists and specialists in addition to a strong range of other relevant language and cultural services listed at the bottom of the page. ',about_commit:'Committed to the worldwide success of our customers',about_expert:'Our work brings language experts and expertise together',about_expert_details:'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur. Et a nisi venenatis elementum elementum faucibus at. Euismod cras vitae in enim aliquam condimentum imperdiet. Vitae ut vestibulum est justo id massa cursus nibh. Fermentum amet nunc integer ut suspendisse congue ac sed. Tincidunt eu congue tortor mauris orci. Vestibulum risus facilisis sit sed praesent urna. Imperdiet congue viverra odio malesuada.',about_info:'Who are we?',about_info_details:'SprogTeam was established in 2015 by Claude Shukuru Munyamanzi and is owned by AATS, a well-established interpretation bureau, seeking to provide interpretation and translation in every variety and language, to whomever may need it. SprogTeam consists of hundreds of freelancers and language experts, in addition to the professional team, making sure that everything runs as smoothly as possible, to accommodate your specific needs. If you want to learn more about us or if you have any questions regarding our work, please do not hesitate to contact us via the contact formula down below.',about_ourwork:'At Sprogteam we work to bring language experts and expertise together',about_ourwork_details:'We work hard to accommodate your needs when it comes to translation and interpretation solutions. With our 400+ freelancers and language experts, skilled in more than 60 different languages and dialects, we bring language experts to any expertise you may need.',contact_text:'Tell us your needs and we\u2019ll contact you within 24 hours!',added:'Added',assignment:'Assignment',needed:'Needed',estimated:'Estimated',budget:'Budget',currency:'Currency',created:'Created',deleted:'Deleted',medical_translation:'Medical translation',technical_translation:'Technical translation',oral:'Orally',both:'Both',language_manager:'Language Management',pending:'Pending',archive:'Archive',translation_handbook:'Translation handbook',translation:'Translation',tasks:'opgaver',create_a_gig:'Create a Gig',gigs:'Gigs',get_started:'Get Started',available_services:'Available Services',team_colaboration:'Team collaborations',become_part:'Become part of our Language Team!',become_part_body:'Do you want to be part of our dynamic team, where we work with languages and provide quality services in interpretation, translation, copywriting and proofreading? In order to become part of the theme, there are some conditions that must be met.',become_part_condition:'Below are the conditions that must be met in order to become part of Sprogteam',clean_record:"Clean criminal record and children's record",clean_record_body:"We give high priority to safety and trust. Therefore, we require that our team members can present a clean criminal record and children's certificate.",bilingua:'Bilingual skills',bilingua_body:'For our translation department, it is necessary to be bilingual and have a deep understanding of both languages.',experience:'Experience',translation_area:'Translation areas',experience_body:'We are looking for experienced translators/interpreters who have worked with this in practice and thereby gained experience in this area for a longer period, as we as a company want to ensure high quality and expertise.',marketing_translation:'Marketing translation',written_trans_condition:'If you are applying for a position as a written translator, the following requirements must also be met:',written_trans_condition_body:"Linguistic higher education or at least 1 year of experience with written translations.\n\nA language higher education is essential to ensure professional expertise within our services.\n\nWe are looking for experienced written translators with a minimum of 1 year of practical experience to ensure high quality and expertise.",copy_writter:'For those of you who are copywriters',copy_writter_body:'A skilled copywriter must not only be a master of writing, but also an expert in understanding the needs, feelings and passion of others. We are looking for copywriters who can convey messages in an engaging and targeted way.',proof_read:'For those of you who can proofread',proof_read_body:'We are also looking for professional proofreaders who can ensure that the texts are error-free and meet the highest standards of language use and grammar.',others_text:"If you meet these requirements and are ready to be part of Sprogteam, we are very interested in hearing from you! Send us your application and let's create language quality together!\n\nIf you have any questions or need further information, please feel free to contact us.",career:'Career',home:'Home',change:'Change',author:'Author',trans_cert:'Translation of certificate',criminal_cert:'interpretation in criminal proceedings',marriage_cert:'Marriage certificate',judge_cert:'judgments translation',edu_cert:'Education documents',filter_header:'Find your interpreter here',filter_subheader:'If the desired language is not listed, please contact us.',new_translator_brief:"Sign up as an interpreter, effortlessly create gigs, and start earning \u2013 it's that simple! With our user-friendly platform, you can quickly join our community, showcase your skills, and begin accepting interpretation opportunities.",new_user_brief:'Create your user account in just minutes! As an interpreter, you can easily sign up, create gigs, and kickstart your earning journey. Our intuitive platform allows you to seamlessly join our community, highlight your expertise, and start accepting interpretation opportunities right away. Join us today and take the first step towards a rewarding career as an interpreter!',get_a_quote:'Get a Quote',proceed_next:'Proceed Next',approval:'Approval',category:'Category',pay_text:'You will get paid',record:'record',for:'for',checkout:'Checkout',create_account_text:"Don't have an account",order_anonymous_interpreter:'Order Anonymous Interpreter',message_to_citizen:'Message to citizen',verified:'Verified',prefered_sex:'Prefer specific gender?',citizen_phone:"Citizen's telephone number",deleteTitle:'Are you sure?',deleteBody:'Are you sure you want delete your account?'}},1831,[]);
